    RefIds:
    - rid: 1000
      type: {class: BtRoot, ns: CGD.BehaviorTrees, asm: CGD.Runtime}
      data:
        _guid: ee7696869a6d413ead9ebb2c4d141e61
        _position: {x: 0, y: 0}
        _comment: 'TECH siege (sentinel): not a tank but the squad''s siege engine, a slow, heavily plated machine that holds its own post well behind the other Tech, 12 m behind the ally nearest the threat in high cover, and makes cover useless to the enemy. When a target ducks behind cover or into a bush it shells the spot with a Mortar Shell every 5 s (no line of sight needed), pours suppressing fire into it between shells and watches it for the target breaking cover; a target in the open gets a Missile Salvo (Signature) to drive it back into hiding where the mortar finds it. Otherwise it covers the field from its post with suppressing fire. It grenades anything within 12 m, Fortifies under fire (Boost) and bashes what reaches it (Special). Kit: Signature (Missile Salvo), Boost (Fortify), Special (Weapon Bash), Grenade (Tech Grenade); the Mortar Shell is set on the tree.'
        _children:
        - 0b4288b1429442c3b18396dfde494b48
